ns-processing}.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md`\n\n**Implementation**:\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (`_try_create_github_issue`, `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`, `add_item`)\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (`backlog_add` MCP tool, docstring only)\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tool_responses.py` (`BacklogAddResponse` \u2014 verified unchanged, as spec required)\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` (CLI `add` command)\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py`\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py`\n\n## Findings by Category\n\n### 1. Documented but Unimplemented (Critical)\n\nNone found. Every contract described in the architect spec's Component Contracts\nsection (`_try_create_github_issue`, `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`, `add_item`,\n`BacklogAddResponse`, MCP `backlog_add`, CLI `backlog add`) has a matching diff\nin the working tree (verified via `git diff main` against each file), and all\ndiffs match the spec's prescribed signatures and return-tuple shapes exactly.\n\n### 2. Implemented but Undocumented (High)\n\nNone found. `operations.add_item`'s new `error` result key is documented in its\nown docstring (the `Returns:` block addition matches the spec verbatim) and in\n`backlog_core/server.py`'s `backlog_add` docstring (the `On error, error is set`\nsentence gained the exact clause the spec specified). The CLI's new non-zero\nexit path (`sam_schema/backlog.py:74-77`) is covered by a new test\n(`test_add_exits_nonzero_when_result_carries_an_error_without_raising`,\n`sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py`) that was not explicitly named in the\nspec's test contract but adds correct coverage \u2014 not drift, additional rigor.\n\n### 3. Outdated Documentation (Medium)\n\nNone found. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`\nStep 5, \"Error handling\", and \"Completion criteria\" sections were all updated\n(commit `074d0ac0a`, refined by `51823112c`) to describe the new\nstored-with-error-vs-never-stored distinction. The refinement in `51823112c`\n(checking for a non-empty `reference`/`file_path`/`title` to distinguish \"item\nstored, issue creation failed\" from \"item never stored, e.g. duplicate/validation\nerror raised before any write\") is a design refinement beyond the architect\nspec's literal text but consistent with it \u2014 the spec's own Concern #1 already\nestablished that only the \"obtained a GitHub client but creation failed\"\nsub-case populates `error` on a stored item; the doc's added branch correctly\nhandles the pre-existing `except BacklogError` raise path (nothing stored) as a\nseparate case. Documentation and code agree.\n\n`docs/backlog-lifecycle.md:344` (\"`backlog_add` returns success with `item_ref`\")\ndescribes only the happy-path transition and is unaffected by this fix \u2014 the\nhappy path is unchanged. Not drift.\n\n### 4. Mismatched Details (Low)\n\nNone found.\n\n## Consumer Sweep (beyond architect spec's Impact Radius)\n\nSearched all `.md` files under `plugins/development-harness` for `backlog_add`\nand `item_ref`/`error` co-occurrence to independently verify the spec's claim\n(\"no other skill/agent/hook reads `add_item`/`backlog_add`'s `item_ref` or\n`error` fields\"):\n\n- `skills/complete-implementation/references/{recursive-follow-up-handling,concerns-processing}.md` \u2014\n  call `backlog_add` but never inspect its `item_ref`/`error` return fields.\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` \u2014 its `item_ref`\n  occurrences refer to the *input* argument name (the request payload), not\n  `backlog_add`'s response field. Unrelated, confirmed by reading context lines